@startuml fig_decision_tree
!include _style.puml
' Book figure — the decision path of Chapter 2, in the order the decisions bind.
' Form: decision tree. Evidence status: conceptual illustration — it orders the
' book's own recommendations and asserts no measured value. The recommendations
' it orders are carried by the claim cards in the chapters it points to.
title the decision path

rectangle "1. What must the schema answer —\nafter an undo, a cancellation,\na correction?" as D1
rectangle "2. Can the current representation\nanswer it? If not, change the\nrepresentation before the speed." as D2
rectangle "3. Is there a contended row\nor a hot drop?" as D3
rectangle "4. If not: leave the row canonical\nand index the question." as D4
rectangle "5. If yes: arbitrate it — conditional\nupdate, lock plus invariant recheck,\nor pre-created rows." as D5
rectangle "6. Is any read derived? Name the\nmaintainer, the transaction it\nshares, and the freshness contract." as D6
rectangle "7. State the evidence level and the\ngap before quoting any number." as D7

D1 --> D2
D2 --> D3
D3 --> D4
D3 --> D5
D4 --> D6
D5 --> D6
D6 --> D7
@enduml
